WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.901
- All the best foods are
eaten with your hands.

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:02.734
- Yeah.

00:00:02.734 --> 00:00:04.699
- Everyone knows that, and
people who don't know that

00:00:04.699 --> 00:00:05.907
are wrong.

00:00:05.907 --> 00:00:08.891
(bright calypso music)

00:00:08.891 --> 00:00:10.702
- [Man] I've never had Nigerian
food, I've always wanted

00:00:10.702 --> 00:00:12.455
to try it and I'm excited.

00:00:12.455 --> 00:00:15.705
(bright calypso music)

00:00:21.885 --> 00:00:24.471
- This meat's a little
chewy which I really like.

00:00:24.471 --> 00:00:25.802
- Tastes like spaghetti.

00:00:25.802 --> 00:00:27.127
- It does!

00:00:27.127 --> 00:00:28.704
Like, better than spaghetti.

00:00:28.704 --> 00:00:31.408
- It's like if sweet
potato fries had a cousin

00:00:31.408 --> 00:00:32.772
and that cousin was better.

00:00:32.772 --> 00:00:35.272
(light music)

00:00:37.411 --> 00:00:39.617
- The lady back here
wonderfully explained that it's

00:00:39.617 --> 00:00:41.747
very customary to do this which
makes sense because you're

00:00:41.747 --> 00:00:42.861
eating from your hand.

00:00:42.861 --> 00:00:44.324
- Okay, you're a pro.

00:00:44.324 --> 00:00:46.269
- I just cheated, I
watched other people do it.

00:00:46.269 --> 00:00:48.202
- A lot of times in America
we get so used to just, like,

00:00:48.202 --> 00:00:50.164
fork and knives kind of
shoving it into your mouth

00:00:50.164 --> 00:00:52.872
all the time, whereas, this
is more of like a full-on

00:00:52.872 --> 00:00:53.730
experience.

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:55.818
- All the best foods are
eaten with your hands.

00:00:55.818 --> 00:00:57.553
Is there a fishiness I detect?

00:00:57.553 --> 00:00:59.034
- A little, I get that too.

00:00:59.034 --> 00:01:02.598
- It's like tangy, sharp,
it tastes like tofu-ish.

00:01:02.598 --> 00:01:04.560
- Kind of just like really
starchy, overcooked rice

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:08.345
in like a mashed potato, but
with this together it has

00:01:08.345 --> 00:01:10.017
so much more flavor.

00:01:10.017 --> 00:01:11.561
- I love all meats on sticks.

00:01:11.561 --> 00:01:13.639
I've never had a meat
on stick I didn't like.

00:01:13.639 --> 00:01:15.729
- It's like a powdery
flavor on the outside.

00:01:15.729 --> 00:01:17.691
Very beef jerky-ish also.

00:01:17.691 --> 00:01:20.122
- It's one of those things
where it's, it is hot,

00:01:20.122 --> 00:01:23.863
but as you keep eating it
you just kind of burn off

00:01:23.863 --> 00:01:27.490
your feelers a bit so
it's easier to eat it.

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:29.162
- [Man] It's like
addicting, like hot Cheetos.

00:01:29.162 --> 00:01:30.114
- Mmm-hmm, Mmm-hmm.

00:01:30.114 --> 00:01:32.405
This is really opening up my sinuses.

00:01:32.405 --> 00:01:34.286
It snapped me out of my food coma.

00:01:34.286 --> 00:01:36.689
(big band music)

00:01:36.689 --> 00:01:39.642
- [Man] It's a lot of like,
it's like salty and spicy.

00:01:39.642 --> 00:01:42.670
- Like the Midwestern in me
wants to get like a big ass roll

00:01:42.670 --> 00:01:43.674
and just dunk it.

00:01:43.674 --> 00:01:45.930
- I'm not a big seafood guy
but this is like a good level

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:46.882
of fishiness.

00:01:46.882 --> 00:01:49.053
- I also can tell that they
roasted the peppers beforehand

00:01:49.053 --> 00:01:50.271
which is really great.

00:01:50.271 --> 00:01:52.175
Give it some great, deep flavor.

00:01:52.175 --> 00:01:53.221
- I'm sweating.

00:01:53.221 --> 00:01:54.301
- Wow.

00:01:54.301 --> 00:01:57.146
It like hits you in a wave of heat.

00:01:57.146 --> 00:01:58.205
- I can't even speak.

00:01:58.205 --> 00:01:59.980
- It's kind of comforting,
like comforting food.

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:01.537
- It's for sure comforting, yeah.

00:02:01.537 --> 00:02:02.370
- [Woman] This was delicious.

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:04.943
I had a great time eating all
that and I wish it was more

00:02:04.943 --> 00:02:08.484
mainstream so I can eat
that jollof rice anywhere.

00:02:08.484 --> 00:02:09.613
It was so good.

00:02:09.613 --> 00:02:11.765
- A lot of our cultures around the world,

00:02:11.765 --> 00:02:14.861
especially foodwise, have stemmed
from there and I feel like

00:02:14.861 --> 00:02:17.578
it's just been a great experience
that we're missing out on.

00:02:17.578 --> 00:02:20.911
(bright calypso music)

